{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5513) to implement `cmd/base32/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. The task is specifically scoped to srd079-base32 requirements R1.1 through R1.4 (encoding functionality only, NOT decoding). The task requires creating a single file that implements Base32 encoding using the shared `pkg/encutil` library, with SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys`. The execution constitution explicitly forbids scope creep, git commands, and reading files already provided in the prompt context.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - RFC 4648 Base32 encoding using Go's `encoding/base32.StdEncoding`\n   - Shared encoding library `pkg/encutil` with `Encode()`, `EncoderConfig`, and `OpenInput()` functions\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing pattern against GNU reference binary (`gbase32`)\n   - Cobbler-scaffold pipeline: measure → stitch code generation cycle\n   - Line wrapping at 76 characters default, configurable via `-w`/`--wrap` flag\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for errors\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd079-base32.yaml` (READ)\n     - Contains full SRD with R1 (Encoding), R2 (Decoding), R3 (Exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - Only R1.1-R1.4 are in scope for this task\n     - R1.1: Read from FILE/stdin, encode RFC 4648 Base32, write to stdout\n     - R1.2: Wrap at 76 chars per line by default\n     - R1.3: `-w COLS`/`--wrap=COLS` sets wrap column; `-w 0` disables wrapping\n     - R1.4: Exit 1 when named file cannot be opened, print error to stderr\n     - Non-goals: No Base32hex, no Base64\n\n   - `pkg/encutil/encode.go` (PROVIDED in prompt context)\n     - `EncoderConfig struct { Encode func([]byte) string; WrapCol int }`\n     - `func Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error` - reads all input, encodes, writes wrapped\n     - `writeWrapped()` helper handles line wrapping logic\n\n   - `pkg/encutil/decode.go` (PROVIDED in prompt context)\n     - `DecoderConfig struct { Decode func(string) ([]byte, error); IgnoreGarbage bool }`\n     - `func Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error`\n     - `func OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)` - returns stdin for \"\" or \"-\", otherwise opens file\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED in prompt context)\n     - `func InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - installs SIGPIPE handler that exits 0\n\n   - `cmd/base32/main.go` (TO BE CREATED)\n     - Must implement R1.1-R1.4 encoding functionality\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n     - Must use `encutil.Encode` with `base32.StdEncoding.EncodeToString`\n     - Must use `encutil.OpenInput` for file/stdin handling\n\n   - `cmd/base32/base32_test.go` (EXISTS in repo but content not provided)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read and analyzed the SRD to understand the full requirement scope\n   - Determined that only R1.1-R1.4 (encoding) is in scope, NOT R2.x (decoding) per task title and acceptance criteria\n   - Identified the correct pkg/encutil API functions to use (Encode, EncoderConfig, OpenInput)\n   - Identified that `encoding/base32.StdEncoding.EncodeToString` should be used as the Encode function in EncoderConfig\n   - Default wrap column is 76 per R1.2\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task prompt containing the full stitch task description, project context, SRDs, source code, execution constitution, go style constitution, design decisions, acceptance criteria, and constraints. The task is to implement cmd/base32/main.go with srd079-base32 R1.1-R1.4.\n   - Second m